- Phase 18 audit still says P18-V01 PARTIAL and has no current-revision GitHub Ubuntu workflow result. The local P18-V02 rerun is recorded passing on f3d5b44d.
- Pinned Java 5.5.1 source shows DefaultMQProducerImpl.shutdown(boolean) calls MQClientInstance.unregisterProducer(current facade group); MQClientInstance removes by that group key. Rust Producer::shutdown currently unregisters the original GroupLease. This is a source-confirmed non-manual behavior mismatch; implement a fixture-backed differential before changing lifecycle behavior.
- P15 matrix currently claims owner-scoped pending-request drain on producer shutdown. Source review of RequestFutureHolder.shutdown(DefaultMQProducerImpl) shows it only removes the producer from producerSet and stops the global timeout scanner when the set becomes empty; it does not remove pending requests or notify callbacks. Track this as a separate source-confirmed P15/P18 parity finding; do not conceal it as an accepted difference.

